── WHAT THIS INSTRUMENT CANNOT SEE, MEASURED ──
Running deepblend/tests/e2e/ui.e2e.mjs with NODE_V8_COVERAGE produces ZERO reports for the host
package: the `dsh web` process it starts does not write them. So every path reached only through
the UI reads as dark here. That is why listProjects, getRevisionDetail, getQaRecord and readArtifact
report count 0 — the browser suite exercises all four end to end (the panel lists projects, opens a
revision, shows QA, and fetches artifact bytes), and the routes that call them are served by that
invisible process.

    listProjects        0        getScene      6
    getRevisionDetail   0        listJobs      8
    readArtifact        0        getQaRecord   0

Read a dark line as "no test I can see executes this", not as "nothing executes this".

── WHAT THE READING SAYS ──
Of the 13.7%, most is error handling: catch blocks, "the encoder is missing" fallbacks, the
unreadable-record branch of the reconciler, the torn-journal-line branch. That is the expected
shape — an error path runs only when something goes wrong, and a suite that made every error path
run would be a suite that breaks things on purpose (which is what the round-22 disk probe did, by
hand, for one of them).

The interesting rows are the whole bodies that are dark for a different reason: they are reachable
only from a process this instrument cannot see. That is a fact about the measurement, and it is
written down here rather than left to be inferred from a number.
